;; spec:   stdlib §2.1 rule 4 (count is size: O(1) on Map, Set and Array), §8.1 item 5 (count cases)
;; expect: accept
;; result: 0
;; audit:  clean
;; allocs: <= 5
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; The size of a Map, a Set or an Array is read from the structure, not by a walk, and nth and last of an Array
;; are indexes: a walk through each-while would build a pair or a closure and a cell per call, and a pair per
;; entry on a Map, so the count of heap objects tells the two apart. The inputs are `def`s (a def is not in the
;; trace, so a map of 300 entries costs the run nothing): a Map of 10 and of 300 entries, a Set of 300 keys, an
;; Array of 1000, made in main. The run allocates the Checks (3 objects), the array and the one Option that
;; `last` returns, and nothing for any count or nth, whatever the size.
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq tl.check))

(def small: (Map i64 i64) {0 0 1 1 2 4 3 9 4 16 5 25 6 36 7 49 8 64 9 81})
(def big: (Map i64 i64) {0 0 1 1 2 4 3 9 4 16 5 25 6 36 7 49 8 64 9 81 10 100 11 121 12 144 13 169 14 196 15 225 16 256 17 289 18 324 19 361 20 400 21 441 22 484 23 529 24 576 25 625 26 676 27 729 28 784 29 841 30 900 31 961 32 1024 33 1089 34 1156 35 1225 36 1296 37 1369 38 1444 39 1521 40 1600 41 1681 42 1764 43 1849 44 1936 45 2025 46 2116 47 2209 48 2304 49 2401 50 2500 51 2601 52 2704 53 2809 54 2916 55 3025 56 3136 57 3249 58 3364 59 3481 60 3600 61 3721 62 3844 63 3969 64 4096 65 4225 66 4356 67 4489 68 4624 69 4761 70 4900 71 5041 72 5184 73 5329 74 5476 75 5625 76 5776 77 5929 78 6084 79 6241 80 6400 81 6561 82 6724 83 6889 84 7056 85 7225 86 7396 87 7569 88 7744 89 7921 90 8100 91 8281 92 8464 93 8649 94 8836 95 9025 96 9216 97 9409 98 9604 99 9801 100 10000 101 10201 102 10404 103 10609 104 10816 105 11025 106 11236 107 11449 108 11664 109 11881 110 12100 111 12321 112 12544 113 12769 114 12996 115 13225 116 13456 117 13689 118 13924 119 14161 120 14400 121 14641 122 14884 123 15129 124 15376 125 15625 126 15876 127 16129 128 16384 129 16641 130 16900 131 17161 132 17424 133 17689 134 17956 135 18225 136 18496 137 18769 138 19044 139 19321 140 19600 141 19881 142 20164 143 20449 144 20736 145 21025 146 21316 147 21609 148 21904 149 22201 150 22500 151 22801 152 23104 153 23409 154 23716 155 24025 156 24336 157 24649 158 24964 159 25281 160 25600 161 25921 162 26244 163 26569 164 26896 165 27225 166 27556 167 27889 168 28224 169 28561 170 28900 171 29241 172 29584 173 29929 174 30276 175 30625 176 30976 177 31329 178 31684 179 32041 180 32400 181 32761 182 33124 183 33489 184 33856 185 34225 186 34596 187 34969 188 35344 189 35721 190 36100 191 36481 192 36864 193 37249 194 37636 195 38025 196 38416 197 38809 198 39204 199 39601 200 40000 201 40401 202 40804 203 41209 204 41616 205 42025 206 42436 207 42849 208 43264 209 43681 210 44100 211 44521 212 44944 213 45369 214 45796 215 46225 216 46656 217 47089 218 47524 219 47961 220 48400 221 48841 222 49284 2